ready1_open_rewrite.raw_answer_text:
\textbf{Solution:} Substitute B ($-3$, $0$) and C ($0$, $3$) into $y=-x^2+bx+c$, yielding
\[
\left\{
\begin{array}{l}
-9-3b+c=0 \\
c=3
\end{array}
\right.
\]
Therefore,
\[
\left\{
\begin{array}{l}
b=-2 \\
c=3
\end{array}
\right.
\]
Therefore, the equation of the parabola is: \boxed{y=-x^2-2x+3}.

